 "note": "NFCI ALFRED vintages for the IC12 confirmation study. ALFRED's NFCI archive begins 2011-05-25 (every earlier vintage_date returns HTTP 404); FRED's own graph CSV ignores vintage_date, so ALFRED is the only source. The raw per-vintage response bytes are not committed (800 files); each vintage's SHA-256 of the raw ALFRED response is in the `sha256_raw` column of ic12_confirm_v1_nfci_vintage_dates.csv, next to the row count and observation range that response parsed to. ic12_confirm_v1_nfci_live.csv was re-downloaded next to the committed data/historical/plugins_c2_nfci.csv: the two files carry the same 2,910 (date, value) pairs but different headers (`observation_date,NFCI` vs `date,value`), so the value comparison, not the byte comparison, is the check."
